Subject: [PATCH 0004] Prism keychain service name (Prism Safe Storage)

OSCrypt on macOS stores its encryption password in the login keychain item
"<product> Safe Storage". Upstream keys this off GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING only,
so the Chromium slot keeps using "Chromium Safe Storage". That item's ACL
trusts the Chromium.app binary that created it; after the rebrand to
Prism.app (patch 0003) the renamed binary is no longer trusted, so macOS
posts an interactive keychain prompt. Unattended (agent-driven) runs never
answer it: OSCrypt blocks, the cookie store's DB key load never completes,
and every web navigation stalls in URLRequestHttpJob::AddCookieHeaderAndStart
(chrome:// and data: URLs still work because they skip the cookie path).
Debugged via netlog: page URL_REQUESTs park right after
COMPUTED_PRIVACY_MODE and are torn down at shutdown.

"Prism Safe Storage" does not exist in any keychain yet, so first use
creates it under our own identity without any prompt.

diff --git a/components/os_crypt/common/keychain_password_mac.mm b/components/os_crypt/common/keychain_password_mac.mm
index f240dc22ee..90460803bf 100644
--- a/components/os_crypt/common/keychain_password_mac.mm
+++ b/components/os_crypt/common/keychain_password_mac.mm
@@ -38,8 +38,15 @@
 const char kDefaultServiceName[] = "Chrome Safe Storage";
 const char kDefaultAccountName[] = "Chrome";
 #else
-const char kDefaultServiceName[] = "Chromium Safe Storage";
-const char kDefaultAccountName[] = "Chromium";
+// Prism: the fork's Chromium-branding slot is our product surface (patch
+// 0003). Use Prism's own keychain item: reusing "Chromium Safe Storage" would
+// make macOS gate access on that item's ACL (created by the old Chromium.app
+// binary), posting an interactive prompt that hangs unattended automation —
+// the cookie store key load then blocks forever and every web navigation
+// stalls in AddCookieHeaderAndStart. A fresh "Prism Safe Storage" item is
+// created by first use without any prompt.
+const char kDefaultServiceName[] = "Prism Safe Storage";
+const char kDefaultAccountName[] = "Prism";
 #endif
 
